  "dom_id": "step-q74579",
  "name": "Question 17",
  "problem": "Simplify $\\frac{\\operatorname{csc}\u2061\\theta +1}{{cot}^{2}\u2061\\theta }.$",
  "worked_solution": "First, let's recall the following identity: \n\n$$\n{cot}^{2}\u2061\\theta ={csc}^{2}\u2061\\theta -1\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above identity into the given expression, and then factoring it as a difference of squares, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{csc}\u2061\\theta +1}{{cot}^{2}\u2061\\theta } & =\\frac{\\operatorname{csc}\u2061\\theta +1}{{csc}^{2}\u2061\\theta -1} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{csc}\u2061\\theta +1}{(\\operatorname{csc}\u2061\\theta +1)(\\operatorname{csc}\u2061\\theta -1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{\\operatorname{csc}\u2061\\theta +1}}{\\cancel{(\\operatorname{csc}\u2061\\theta +1)}(\\operatorname{csc}\u2061\\theta -1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{csc}\u2061\\theta -1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
